{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:8083169 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:8083169 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"8083169","source":"MED","pmid":"8083169","pmcid":"PMC196781","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC196781"]},"doi":"10.1128/jb.176.18.5771-5779.1994","title":"Characterization of the pcaR regulatory gene from Pseudomonas putida, which is required for the complete degradation of p-hydroxybenzoate.","authorString":"Romero-Steiner S, Parales RE, Harwood CS, Houghton JE.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Romero-Steiner S","lastName":"Romero-Steiner","firstName":"S","initials":"S","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biology, Georgia State University, Atlanta 30303."}]}},{"fullName":"Parales RE","lastName":"Parales","firstName":"R E","initials":"RE"},{"fullName":"Harwood CS","lastName":"Harwood","firstName":"C S","initials":"CS"},{"fullName":"Houghton JE","lastName":"Houghton","firstName":"J E","initials":"JE"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","related_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"18","volume":"176","journalIssueId":803327,"dateOfPublication":"1994 Sep","monthOfPublication":9,"yearOfPublication":1994,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"J Bacteriol","title":"Journal of bacteriology","essn":"1098-5530","issn":"0021-9193","nlmid":"2985120R","isoabbreviation":"J Bacteriol"},"printPublicationDate":"1994-09-01"},"pubYear":"1994","pageInfo":"5771-5779","abstractText":"The pca branch of the beta-ketoadipate pathway in Pseudomonas putida is responsible for the complete degradation of p-hydroxybenzoate through ortho cleavage of the initial pathway metabolite, protocatechuate. The pcaR regulatory locus has been found to be required for both induction of all of the genes within the pca regulon (pcaBDC, pcaIJ, and pcaF) and the chemotactic response of the bacteria to aromatic compounds. Insertional inactivation mutagenesis, using Tn5 and mini-Tn5 transposons, was used to locate, clone, and sequence this pcaR regulatory gene. The pcaR gene product, when overexpressed in Escherichia coli, possessed a specific affinity for the pcaIJ promoter region and demonstrated that the entire PcaR protein was required for this function. The deduced amino acid sequence of the PcaR regulatory peptide bears little resemblance to its counterpart in the other branch of the pathway, CatR, but exhibits significant homology to its regulatory antecedent, PobR, which regulates the initial breakdown of p-hydroxybenzoate into protocatechuate. Comparisons of the pcaIJ and pcaR promoter regions revealed conservation of a 15-bp sequence centered around the -10 region in both sequences. This, together with previously defined deletional studies with the pcaIJ promoter region, suggests that PcaR exerts its regulatory effect through protein-DNA interactions within this region, which would be unusually close to the transcriptional start site of pcaIJ for a positive regulator.","affiliation":"Department of Biology, Georgia State University, Atlanta 30303.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, U.S. Gov't, P.H.S.","Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","research-article","Research Support, U.S. Gov't, Non-P.H.S.","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"NIGMS NIH HHS","acronym":"GM","grantId":"GM08365","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Pseudomonas putida","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Parabens","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Bacterial Proteins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbrevia